{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0127UQQVTXbC2XTunVPxZFhs","type":"tool_result","content":"README.md\nscripts/deploy.sh\nsrc/assets/logo.png\nsrc/assets/mark.svg\nsrc/booking.js\nsrc/clases.html\nsrc/index.html\nsrc/styles.css\n=== README.md\n# ruta-ceramica site\n\nStatic site for a ceramics studio: plain HTML, one CSS file, one JS file\n(the class booking widget). Hosted on S3 behind CloudFront.\n\n- `src/` — the site as served (no build step; `scripts/deploy.sh` copies it up)\n- `scripts/deploy.sh` — upload to the bucket and invalidate CloudFront\n\nDeploy: `./scripts/deploy.sh` (needs AWS CLI configured with the studio profile).\n\nKnown problem: after a deploy, returning visitors keep running the old\n`booking.js` for days. The CloudFront invalidation runs every time, but\nbrowsers never ask again, because the objects are uploaded with no\n`Cache-Control` header at all.\n=== scripts/deploy.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Upload src/ to the bucket and invalidate CloudFront.\nset -euo pipefail\ncd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\"\n\nBUCKET=\"ruta-ceramica-site-7f3a\"\nDISTRIBUTION_ID=\"E2QX9ZK1DEMO01\"\nPROFILE=\"studio\"\n\naws s3 sync src/ \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --delete --profile \"$PROFILE\"\n\naws cloudfront create-invalidation --distribution-id \"$DISTRIBUTION_ID\" \\\n  --paths \"/*\" --profile \"$PROFILE\" > /dev/null\n\necho \"deployed\"\n=== src/assets/mark.svg\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#b5651d\"/></svg>\n=== src/booking.js\n// Class booking widget: shows the next slots and a WhatsApp link.\n(function () {\n  var slots = [\n    { day: \"sábado\", time: \"10:00\", seats: 2 },\n    { day: \"martes\", time: \"18:30\", seats: 4 }\n  ];\n  var root = document.getElementById(\"booking\");\n  if (!root) return;\n  var html = \"<h2>Próximas clases</h2><ul>\";\n  slots.forEach(function (s) {\n    html += \"<li>\" + s.day + \" \" + s.time + \" · \" + s.seats + \" lugares</li>\";\n  });\n  html += \"</ul><a href='https://wa.me/5491100000000?text=Hola'><button>Reservar por WhatsApp</button></a>\";\n  root.innerHTML = html;\n})();\n=== src/clases.html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"es\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Clases</title><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css\"></head>\n<body><h1>Clases</h1><ul><li>Torno inicial, sábados</li><li>Modelado, martes</li></ul><div id=\"booking\"></div><script src=\"/booking.js\"></script></body></html>\n=== src/index.html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"es\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>Ruta Cerámica · clases y taller</title>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n<h1>Ruta Cerámica</h1>\n<p>Clases de torno y modelado en Villa Crespo.</p>\n<div id=\"booking\"></div>\n<script src=\"/booking.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n=== src/styles.css\nbody { font-family: Georgia, serif; max-width: 42rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; color: #2b2b2b; }\nh1 { font-weight: normal; }\n#booking button { padding: .6rem 1rem; }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98815763-d298-47f8-8487-cb41e969f837","uuid":"1c44beb8-2bd2-44bc-a34a-79d1712d2f26","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:39:34.957Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"README.md\nscripts/deploy.sh\nsrc/assets/logo.png\nsrc/assets/mark.svg\nsrc/booking.js\nsrc/clases.html\nsrc/index.html\nsrc/styles.css\n=== README.md\n# ruta-ceramica site\n\nStatic site for a ceramics studio: plain HTML, one CSS file, one JS file\n(the class booking widget). Hosted on S3 behind CloudFront.\n\n- `src/` — the site as served (no build step; `scripts/deploy.sh` copies it up)\n- `scripts/deploy.sh` — upload to the bucket and invalidate CloudFront\n\nDeploy: `./scripts/deploy.sh` (needs AWS CLI configured with the studio profile).\n\nKnown problem: after a deploy, returning visitors keep running the old\n`booking.js` for days. The CloudFront invalidation runs every time, but\nbrowsers never ask again,